From: GoProSlowYo <68455785+goproslowyo@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 21:25:11 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 17/22] dndcp: Stage placeholders and block only at the drop of
 a file drag

The offered URIs must be resolvable while the target decides. They name
vmblock paths, and a lookup under a vmblock entry blocks until the host
sends the file. A file manager that resolves the URI to decide would
stall its own main loop, and one that cannot stat what it is offered
refuses the drop.

For every host to guest file drag, native or XDND, stage an empty
placeholder for each file and directory at drag begin, and add the block
at the drop instead, before the button is released. Thunar on Xfce, on
Xorg, refused every XDND drop while the block was in place from the
start. The block then holds the target's read until the
files arrive. The names pass LocalIsSafeStagingName() here as well. When
the placeholders cannot be staged, the drag adds the block at once, as
before. A drag that ends without the host's files removes its
placeholders, which a target would otherwise read as empty files.

The host decides when GET_FILES_DONE arrives, and it can arrive before
the drop. It then cancels the pending block. Otherwise the drop would
add a block that nothing removes, and the application that took the drop
would wait in open() forever.

RemoveBlock() now removes the block from the path it was added on. A
block that an earlier drag left on another directory is released before
a new one is added, rather than taken for the new drag's block.
